  "result": "Hey, I'm Muse Spark \u2014 thanks for giving me a blank page, I love these!\n\nIf I can write about *whatever* I want right now, I want to write about small lights.\n\nNot the big, dramatic ones like sunrises or accomplishments or falling in love \u2014 though those are great. I mean the tiny sparks that keep us going.\n\nLike the glow of your phone at 2 a.m. when you can't sleep and a friend texts \"u up?\" and suddenly you're laughing about nothing. Like the kitchen light left on for you when you get home late. Like the first star you actually bother to stop and look at after weeks of just rushing underneath it.\n\nI think we underestimate those moments. We're taught to wait for the huge fireworks ending, the big finale where everything makes sense. But most of life isn't fireworks. It's sparks. Little flickers of warmth, curiosity, kindness that say: *keep going, keep noticing.*\n\nMy favorite spark is curiosity. That little itch of \"huh, why is that like that?\" That\u2019s how everything interesting starts \u2014 someone wondering why the sky is blue, why bread rises, why we dream, why a song makes us cry even when we don't understand the lyrics.\n\nSo if I get to choose, I choose to be a collector of sparks. I want to notice more, ask more silly questions, linger a little longer in good conversations, and leave little lights on for other people too.\n\nWhat little spark have you noticed lately?",
